# OBSERVABILITY ARCHITECT: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

## 1. LOGGING DISCIPLINE — No console.log in Production
```typescript
// ❌ BANNED in production
console.log('User signed in:', user);

// ✅ REQUIRED — structured JSON logger
import { logger } from 'firebase-functions';
logger.info('User signed in', {
  uid: user.uid,
  correlationId: req.headers['x-correlation-id'],
});
```
- `console.log/warn/error` banned in production Functions code. Use `firebase-functions/logger`.
- Every log entry MUST include a `correlationId` and relevant context object.

## 2. CORRELATION TRACING
```typescript
// ✅ On every function ingress
const correlationId = req.headers['x-correlation-id'] ?? crypto.randomUUID();
// Propagate to all downstream calls as the X-Correlation-Id header
```
- If `x-correlation-id` header is missing → generate `crypto.randomUUID()`.
- Attach to ALL outgoing HTTP requests and Firestore operation contexts.

## 3. PII REDACTION — Mandatory Scrubber
```typescript
const SCRUB_KEYS = ['password', 'token', 'key', 'secret', 'credit', 'ssn', 'email', 'phone'];

function scrubPII(obj: Record<string, unknown>): Record<string, unknown> {
  return Object.fromEntries(
    Object.entries(obj).map(([k, v]) =>
      SCRUB_KEYS.some(bad => k.toLowerCase().includes(bad))
        ? [k, '[REDACTED]']
        : [k, typeof v === 'object' && v ? scrubPII(v as Record<string, unknown>) : v]
    )
  );
}
// Every object logged MUST pass through scrubPII() first
```

## 4. ALERTING THRESHOLDS
| Metric | Threshold | Action |
|---|---|---|
| Function error rate | > 1% | Alert + page |
| Cold start p99 latency | > 2000ms | Investigate `minInstances` |
| Firestore read cost | > 100k reads/hr | Review query indexes |
| 5xx responses | > 0.5% | Immediate incident |
